WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.090
Easy Greek Myths. Pandora's Box.

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:07.916
Long ago, the Greeks told this story about the first woman on earth.

00:00:07.916 --> 00:00:09.559
Her name was Pandora.

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:12.678
The gods made Pandora beautiful and clever.

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:14.798
Each god gave her a present.

00:00:14.798 --> 00:00:19.421
But the king of the gods, Zeus, gave her something strange.

00:00:19.421 --> 00:00:20.710
It was a box.

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:23.137
"You must never open it," he said.

00:00:23.137 --> 00:00:26.401
Pandora married a good man and lived happily.

00:00:26.401 --> 00:00:28.883
But every day she looked at the box.

00:00:28.883 --> 00:00:30.174
What was inside it?

00:00:30.174 --> 00:00:31.949
Why could she not open it?

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:34.805
She tried to forget about it, but she could not.

00:00:34.805 --> 00:00:37.008
She wanted to know more and more.

00:00:37.008 --> 00:00:41.634
One day, when her husband was out, she could not wait any longer.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:44.614
"I will only look for one second," she said.

00:00:44.614 --> 00:00:46.913
She lifted the top of the box.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:51.277
At once, a cloud of small, ugly things flew out.

00:00:51.277 --> 00:00:58.038
They were all the bad things of the world: sickness, pain, hunger, anger and lies.

00:00:58.038 --> 00:01:01.389
Before that day, people had not known any of them.

00:01:01.389 --> 00:01:05.330
Now they flew out of the window and spread over the whole earth.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.481
Pandora shut the box as fast as she could.

00:01:08.481 --> 00:01:11.565
She cried, because she knew what she had done.

00:01:11.565 --> 00:01:14.951
Then she heard a small voice from inside the box.

00:01:14.951 --> 00:01:17.056
"Let me out too," it said.

00:01:17.056 --> 00:01:18.046
"I can help."

00:01:18.046 --> 00:01:22.158
She opened the box again, and one last thing flew out.

00:01:22.158 --> 00:01:25.256
It was small and bright, with soft wings.

00:01:25.256 --> 00:01:26.257
It was hope.

00:01:26.257 --> 00:01:31.280
And so, the Greeks said, people have had many troubles ever since.

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.657
But they have always had hope too.
